how do I Run push_files once with the JSON ?

Use the tool/API call to push_files and pass that JSON as the arguments.

Minimal example (conceptual)

Call:

tool: push_files
arguments: the exact JSON payload I gave you
So it looks like:

JSON
{
  "tool": "push_files",
  "arguments": {
    "owner": "impete",
    "repo": "github-claude-setup-guide",
    "branch": "main",
    "message": "Add standalone browser-based GitHub + Claude Code Setup Course app under docs/",
    "files": [
      { "path": "docs/index.html", "content": "..." },
      { "path": "docs/styles.css", "content": "..." },
      { "path": "docs/app.js", "content": "..." },
      { "path": "docs/data/course.json", "content": "..." }
    ]
  }
}
If you’re doing it in this Copilot chat/tooling flow

Paste the payload in one tool call to push_files.
Ensure:
owner is impete
repo is github-claude-setup-guide
branch is main
all 4 files are in the files array
Execute once.
If you want a local CLI fallback (no tool call)

You can do the same with git manually:

bash
cd github-claude-setup-guide
mkdir -p docs/data
# create files: docs/index.html docs/styles.css docs/app.js docs/data/course.json
git add docs
git commit -m "Add standalone browser-based GitHub + Claude Code Setup Course app under docs/"
git push origin main
If you want, I can now give you a copy/paste-ready single tool invocation block exactly formatted for your environment so you can run it without editing.
